Another possibility.  Treat the wand of polymorph the same as WOW.
At least one in the dungeon somewhere, not reproducable by polypiling.
This would let everyone polypile to get things we need to survive in
Hell that the game doesn't happen to generate without creating impervious
characters.


Another proposal to make the game interesting.  Have the characters "age"
at some faster than normal rate, or consider the time spent as adding
"stress" on your character that would reduce his/her effectiveness.
Have the effect be obvious somehow and  make the characters need to "sleep"
for some small number of turns periodically, treated as eating is, and
have that time increase as the character "ages".  This effect should
overpower the benifit of the different gloves and shoes, the character
should get weak, clumsy, slow down, and be less able to think clearly
enough to successfully cast spells.
             

The game as an endurance contest overpowers the game as a test of skill
and strategy, turning a game into work.  I'd prefer to be forced into
diving down and know everyone else is, rather than having people spending
large amounts of hours gathering stuff.  I get enought of that at work.




